Function Objectsbymodule(m: Handle)
Title: ObjectsByModule(m)
Description: Returns a list of all objects in module m, and its submodules, grouped by module.
Definition: Metavar res := [m];~
Metavar c := Objectsinmod(m);~
IFONLY c = Empty_list THEN res~
ELSE BEGIN~
  Metavar v[] := c DO ( ~
     IF Isamodule(v) AND v <> Excluded_module~
          THEN res := Concat(res, ObjectsByModule(v)) ~
          ELSE res := Concat(res, [v]); 0);~
  res~
END
