Function Indented_modules(m: Handle; nIndents: = 0)
Title: Indented_modules(m)
Description: Returns a list of the titles of the submodules (including m) of the module m, and recursively downwards, indented by nIndents to show the hierarchy.~
It excludes the module in Excluded_module (and any modules it contains).
Definition: VAR indent := (Index i := Sequence(1, nIndents, strict:False); Jointext(Indent_for_Module_Hi, i));~
Metavar res := [indent & (Title OF m)];~
Metavar c := Contains of  m ;~
IF IsNull(c) THEN res~
ELSE BEGIN~
  Metavar v[] := c DO BEGIN ~
     IF Isamodule(v) AND v<>Excluded_module~
          THEN res := Concat(res, Indented_modules(v, nIndents+1)) ELSE 0;~
  END; ~
  res~
END~

