Text Te19
Description: The Analytica Cloud Player (ACP) offers a variety of user-interface styles for navigating models, displaying diagrams, and embedding tables and graphs that go beyond those available in Analytica on the desktop. This library makes it easy to review and select ACP styles and features to an Analytica model. ~
~
HOW TO USE THIS LIBRARY:~
1. Select 'Add library..." from the file menu in Analytica and find this ACP style library.ana to add it into your model.  ~
~
2. Click each button below to open to review and select the Navigation styles, Node styles and Frame nodes that you want in your ACP user interface. Move the cursor over each Node to see more details.~
~
~
~
~
~
3. Click 'Close' when you are finished.~
~
~
4. Select 'Publish to cloud...' from the 'File' menu to upload the model to ACP.~
~
You won't see these styles and options in your model until you run it in ACP -- ~
but this library shows simple illustrations.~
~
Visit the <a href="http://wiki.lumina.com">Analytica wiki</a> for more information about <a href="http://wiki.lumina.com/index.php/Analytica_Cloud_Player">ACP</a> and the <a href="http://wiki.lumina.com/index.php/ACP_Style_Library">ACP Style library</a>
NodeLocation: 280,288,-1
NodeSize: 272,240
NodeInfo: 1,0,0,1,1,1,0,,0,,0
WindState: 2,94,83,634,345

