Variable Sound_impacts
Title: Sound Impacts
Description: Marine mammals are affected by complete removal, if explosives are used, putting the sound impact level at 'Worst'. If no explosives are used and complete removal is selected, then the attribute level is 'Poor' because there remains the potential for noise and vessel traffic impacts on movement, migration, or foraging.. If partial removal is selected,  the attribute level is 'Medium' since there are still negative sound impacts but less compared to complete removal. We assumes no explosives will be used during partial removal. All impacts are conisdered within the overall horizon of our analysis, the period of decommissioning and the ensuing five years. The descriptions, scores and conditions for impacts on marine mammals are provided in Table 4.28 below.
Definition: VAR result := (IF Use_explosives_on_ja = 1 THEN 'Worst' ELSE IF Selected_options_by_ = "No action" THEN 'No action' ELSE 'Poor' )[Comp_rmvl_scenarios=Selected_scenarios];~
IF Result = «null» THEN 'Medium' ELSE result~

NodeLocation: 80,304,1
NodeSize: 72,32
WindState: 2,218,281,887,361
ValueState: 2,62,391,399,222,0,MIDM
ReformVal: [Selected_scenarios,Platforms_to_conside]

Variable Other_short_term_imp
Title: Other short-term impacts on feeding, movement
Description: Short-term impacts of decommissioning include potential increased disturbance of migration and feeding behaviors, which is worse in the case of complete removal compared with partial removal mainly because the equipment will remain on-site for longer in the case of complete removal
Definition: IF Selected_options_by_ = 'No action' THEN 'No action' ELSE ~
IF Selected_options_by_ = '2 Partial platform removal' THEN 'Medium'~
ELSE 'Poor'~

