Variable Water_quality_attrib
Title: Water quality attribute level by platforms considered
Description: This table reflects a combined water quality attribute level level that takes the minimum of the attribute rating (comparitively worst attribute level - for e.g. worst over poor or poor over average) for accidental spills and discharges and shell mound removal~
~
The water quality attribute level for accidental spills and discharges is 'Worst' for complete removal compared to 'Average' for partial removal. For complete removal at shallow depth, the level is 'Poor'. Under complete removal, if shell mounds are removed, then  water quality attribute level is 'Worst'. If shell mounds are not removed  then the attribute level is 'Average' while partial removal results in an 'Average' attribute level.
Definition: IF Benthic_impacts_rati = 'No action' THEN 'No action' ELSE Attribute_level_by_r[Attribute_score=Water_quality_rating]
