Index Hlv_change
Title: HLV change
Description: Computed partial removal factors for each platform based on whether it's going from 4400 HLV to 2000 HLV or any of the other 4 scenarios~
1. 4000-2000~
2. 4000-500~
3. 2000 - 500~
4. 2000 - 4000~
5. 500 - 2000~
6. 500 - 4000~
7. no change
Definition: [2000,3500,1500,-2000,-1500,-3500,0]
NodeLocation: 840,48,1
NodeSize: 48,24
WindState: 2,98,83,594,292
Att_PrevIndexValue: [2000,3500,1500,-2000,-1500,-3500,0]

Variable Input_hlv_day_rate_r
Title: Input HLV day rate removl factor
Description: 7. HLV and support services day rates for partial removal will be factored using a formula that accounts for the reduction in HLV day rates but recognizes that the support services day rates are not affected as significantly.													~
   - Support services day rates vary platform to platform and task to task but typically ranged from $115m-$180m/day in the 2009 report. For factoring purposes, a 													~
    support services day rate of $150m/day was assumed for complete removal and $115m/day for the partial removal as the costs will be at the lower range when working at 85 ft and shallower in the partial removal scenario.													~
    -Gina in <100ft of water was an exception with a support services day rate of only $50m-$70m/day. Gina's HLV factor would be 156+60/204+60=.8182 as compared to the .7655 used for all the platforms; a 5.2% or insignificant error.													~
	Based on the above, adjust the platform structure partial removal cost for the smaller HLV requirement as follows: ~
												~
	4000ton($252m/day) >2000ton($204m/day) =204(HLV day rate)+115(par rem support day rate)/252+150(compl rem support day rate)=319/402=.7935 ~
2000ton>500ton=156+115/204+150=271/354=.7655		~
		4000T>500T=156+115/252+150=..6741 ~
500T>2000T=204+115/156+150=1.0425~
2000T>4000T=252+115/204+150=1.0367~
500T>4000T=252+115/156+150=1.1993
Definition: Table(Hlv_change)(~
0.7935,0.6741,0.7655,1.0367,1.0425,1.1993,1)
